From cce43d24cfc957a55b5c28728634ab7e668bc212 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andras Lasso <lasso@queensu.ca>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:46:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] ENH: Add per-label extent computation and bounds input
 for hierarchy

vtkOrientedImageDataResample::CalculateEffectiveExtentPerLabel finds the
extent of every label of a labelmap in one pass over the voxels.
CalculateEffectiveExtent returns the extent of all non-zero voxels, which
for a shared labelmap (where each segment is one label value) is the
union of all segments, so getting the extent of each segment needed one
masked pass per segment. The label values (in increasing order) and the
extents (six components per label) are returned in vtkIntArray objects,
so the function can be used from Python; the index of a label is found
with vtkIntArray::LookupValue.

vtkTopologicalHierarchy (used for automatic segment opacities) only uses
the bounding boxes of the input poly data, so it now also accepts bounding
boxes directly (SetInputBounds, six components per item), for example
computed from the voxels of each segment of a binary labelmap. Items with
empty bounds neither contain nor are contained by other items, so they
get level 0.

vtkTopologicalHierarchyTest1 tests the per-label extents (including an
empty labelmap and invalid input) and checks that the hierarchy computed
from bounds matches the hierarchy computed from poly data with the same
bounds.
